# T5.4 case 8: Ctrl-R on a tab nobody connected. The run is queued, the
# connection is opened for it, and the rows arrive without a second key.
#
# Also case 9's other half: the same keys against a container that has just
# been started again have to reconnect and answer.

key Tab
type select count(*) as n from bench.customers
key Ctrl-R
expect connecting… then running
frame connecting

wait busy
expect ●
expect 50
frame reconnected-rows
key Ctrl-Q
